{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "D0"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 134, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the input-to-output skip, removing the node2->output edge leaves fewer paths and starves the output."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual where none existed adds a gradient path without sacrificing an existing operation."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling a missing edge 0 reconnects node 1 so edges 2 and 4 become functional."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv where the input-to-node2 edge was absent adds both connectivity and capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing node1->output hurts more when there is no direct input-to-output skip to compensate."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting a 3x3 conv loses more than deleting a skip, pool, or 1x1 conv on the same edge."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring a deep path into the output with a strong op gains more than swapping one existing op for another."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "The input-to-output skip is the key residual path and removing it damages trainability."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a learnable 3x3 conv with parameter-free pooling loses capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3